Or:
Run from itelliJ IDEA CE from LamportClock.java



Summary:
 The implementation of RAFT is this homework is done using Finite State Machine in Akka Actors.

The time out is implemented by setTimer function and the any time out event is handled by a Timeout message sent by the actor to itself. 


Faults/bugs:

1. I try to implement FSM, the framework is the system handles different events, a event consists of a state and a message. However, my program somehow could not decipher what class is the message when an event happens, likely because of the following error: 
ElectionTimeout cannot be cast to java.lang.Class
java.lang.ClassCastException: com.example.Messages$ElectionTimeout cannot be cast to java.lang.Class


2. Most of part of the Figure 2 in the paper is implemented, except for the apply to state machine part. The program is not run successfully because I got stuck at the initial election part, therefore encounter difficulty in further debugging. 



 


